  "authTierOverall": "T1_SIMPLE",
  "authTierRationale": "The endpoint config exposes exactly one credential variant, the CDK's `AccessToken` model, whose only required field is a single secret `access_token` (UI title \"Private App Credentials\"). No OAuth spec is passed (`TokenSource(oauth_spec=None, ...)`), so no OAuth app registration or refresh token is involved. The CDK sends it as `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>` using its DEFAULT_AUTHORIZATION_HEADER / DEFAULT_AUTHORIZATION_TOKEN_TYPE, which the connector does not override. One self-serve API key = T1_SIMPLE.",

  "unionMisfits": [
    {
      "where": "streams[incidents].pull.*.incrementalParam",
      "description": "`incidents` is the only stream that filters server-side, and it does not fit the {param, format} shape: it sends one query parameter `updated_at[date_range]` whose value is a tilde-joined pair of DATES (\"YYYY-MM-DD~YYYY-MM-DD\", inclusive of BOTH bounds) — a two-sided window, not a single since-timestamp. The incremental leg uses cursor..now; the backfill leg uses 1970-01-01..cutoff. Because the parameter is date-granular but the state cursor is a datetime, the connector re-filters every returned record client-side against the exact datetimes. Emitting a one-sided since-param here would change request semantics, so `incrementalParam` is left null on both legs.",
      "proposedShape": {
        "incrementalWindow": {
          "kind": "two_sided_range",
          "param": "updated_at[date_range]",
          "format": "date",
          "separator": "~",
          "boundsInclusive": true,
          "backfillLowerBound": "1970-01-01",
          "clientSideRefilter": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "where": "streams[*].pull.*.params",
      "description": "There is no slot for constant/repeated request params. `incidents` always carries a repeated `mode[one_of]` param with four values (standard, retrospective, test, tutorial) because the API otherwise returns only standard+retrospective. Recorded inside `params` as a JSON array, but that conflates constants with the parent-scoped and windowed values also living in `params`.",
      "proposedShape": {
        "constantParams": { "mode[one_of]": ["standard", "retrospective", "test", "tutorial"] }
      }
    },
    {
      "where": "streams[catalog_entries] / streams[incident_attachments]",
      "description": "Two streams are parent-child but the parent id is sent as a QUERY parameter, not a path placeholder, so `pathPlaceholders` does not apply and the flat stream shape cannot express the dependency. `catalog_entries` runs one paginated sweep per `catalog_type_id` drawn from v3/catalog_types; `incident_attachments` runs one unpaginated GET per `incident_id` drawn from a complete EPOCH..now sweep of v2/incidents (i.e. the full incidents scan is re-run on every 15-minute attachments tick).",
      "proposedShape": {
        "parent": {
          "catalog_entries": { "parentStream": "catalog_types", "parentField": "id", "childParam": "catalog_type_id", "childParamIn": "query" },
          "incident_attachments": { "parentStream": "incidents", "parentField": "id", "childParam": "incident_id", "childParamIn": "query" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "where": "streams[*].supportedSyncModes for the six client-side-filtered incremental streams",
      "description": "catalog_types, custom_fields, incident_statuses, incident_types, incident_roles, severities and catalog_entries are declared incremental and carry an `updated_at` cursor, but they issue an IDENTICAL unfiltered request on every tick and do the incremental filtering purely in Python. The schema cannot distinguish 'server-side incremental' from 'full re-read with client-side cursor filtering' — a materially different cost profile.",
      "proposedShape": { "incrementalFiltering": "client_side" }
    },
    {
      "where": "transports[0].spec.apiVersionPinning",
      "description": "The API version is a path segment but is NOT connector-wide: different streams are pinned to v1, v2 and v3 simultaneously. A single string field cannot express a per-stream version pin.",
      "proposedShape": { "apiVersionPinning": { "kind": "path_segment", "perStream": true } }
    }
  ],

